            "The young church in Thessalonica had a painful question. Some of their members had died, and they were afraid those loved ones would miss the Lord's return. Paul wrote to them with great tenderness: “We do not want you to be uninformed, brothers, about those who are asleep, that you may not grieve as others do who have no hope” (1 Thessalonians 4:13).",
            "May masakit na tanong ang batang iglesia sa Tesalonica. May ilan sa kanilang kasapi ang namatay, at natatakot silang hindi na makakasama ang mga mahal nilang iyon sa pagbabalik ng Panginoon. Sumulat si Pablo sa kanila nang buong lambing: “Mga kapatid, ayaw naming hindi ninyo malaman ang tungkol sa mga natutulog na, upang hindi kayo magdalamhati gaya ng iba na walang pag-asa” (1 Tesalonica 4:13)."
